# Known equivalent changes, kept out on purpose (each guard is also made by something else, so removing it alone changes nothing a caller can see):
#   * the "verified" level in rank_target (a verified profile's rank is at least "verified", whose position is not above itself);
#   * the coalesce to 0 for a profile with no rank in rank_target (only verified profiles are asked about, and they always have one);
#   * the organisation test in profile_badge (a profile with no organisation never matches an organisation's verification);
#   * the "active" test on the profile in job_create (acting as a suspended profile is refused first);
#   * the switch test in verification_request (it ends by asking verification_status, which refuses with the same sentence and takes the whole call back).

